      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need to control the PAM ordering?\n\nAs I understand it, the current PAM order is local authentication followed by remote authentication. However, if the requirement is that a particular user exists only on the remote authentication server, why do we need to perform local authentication first?\n\nConsidering that a BMC typically has a very limited number of local users, even if we perform local authentication first and then fall back to remote authentication, what is the actual additional time incurred by the local authentication step?\n\nIt would be useful to understand the performance impact before adding controls for PAM ordering or is there any other impact?",
      "revId": "267e824dcabb3a26c7bb27b4d34b897ed2593634",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
